 "finding": "the restore changes exactly one thing in the envelope: the clustered corpus HNSW graph, which pg_restore rebuilds. Approximate retrieval over it is 163 % slower and its recall@10 falls from 0.9636 to 0.9410, below the 0.95 floor. Every other shape that looked slower on the restored store was slowed by W3's mutations instead, and on those the restored store is *faster* than the mutated source, because a restore also compacts what mutation left behind",
