 "what_the_first_reading_got_wrong": "that the restore had changed the whole envelope. Three of the seven shapes read the governed store rather than the corpus, and W3 is what changed it: stale_item returned zero rows in W2 and twenty afterwards",
 "why_clustered": "the clustered corpus is the one the recall exit is defined over and the one every mutation wave left alone, so a change in it is a change in the index rather than in the rows",
 "why_it_is_post_hoc": "the control was designed after the restored numbers existed. It decides nothing: all five exit criteria are read from W2's and W1's and W3's sealed measurements, which this record cannot reach. It changes what the wave's finding is *about*"
